title: $:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/doc/Dashboard
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

The main entry point of Projectify is the ''Dashboard''. It provides a unified workspace across your projects and tasks:

* ''{{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/collection}} Projects'' — Your [[Inbox|$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/doc/Inbox]] and active [[Projects|$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/doc/Projects]] (viewed as cards or a list, filterable by [[Category|$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/doc/Categories]]).
* ''{{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/sun}} Today'' — Tasks due or scheduled for today and any overdue items, including a one-click ''Reschedule all to Today'' button.
* ''{{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/calendar-checked}} Upcoming'' — A chronological view of all future scheduled tasks.
* ''{{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/stack}} Next'' — Actionable [[Next actions|$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/doc/NextActions]] across your active projects, with an `@context` filter bar.
* ''{{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/matrix}} Matrix'' — An ''Eisenhower Matrix'' grouping actionable tasks into four quadrants: //Urgent & Important (Do First)//, //Important, Not Urgent (Schedule)//, //Urgent, Less Important (Delegate)//, and //Backlog//.
* ''{{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/review}} Review'' — A ''GTD Weekly Review & Completed Logbook'' showing //Stalled Projects//, //Waiting & Blocked// tasks, //Someday / Maybe// items, and your recently completed tasks.
* ''{{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/images/funnel}} Filter'' — Search and filter open tasks by priority, status, `@context`, or title.

<<py-tip "[[You do not have to use the dashboard|$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/doc/TranscludingUIElements]] to use Projectify, and individual tabs can be toggled in [[Control Panel > Projectify|$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/ui/config/Basics]].">>

The dashboard can be embedded ([[transcluded|https://tiddlywiki.com/#Transclusion]]) in any tiddler using:

```
{{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/ui/dashboard/Dashboard}}
```
<%if [{$:/state/projectify/usage-show-dashboard}match[show]] %>
  <$button class="py-btn btn-primary" set="$:/state/projectify/usage-show-dashboard" setTo="">Hide</$button>
  <hr/>
  {{$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/ui/dashboard/Dashboard}}
  <hr/>
<%else%>
  <$button class="py-btn btn-primary" set="$:/state/projectify/usage-show-dashboard" setTo="show">Show result</$button>
<%endif%>

The dashboard can be customized in many ways, for instance to [[display custom tabs|$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/doc/DashboardCustomTabs]] or [[display the Inbox in a separate tab|$:/plugins/mblackman/projectify/doc/DashboardInboxSeparateTab]].
